USEM - Unsymmetric spectral element method for two-dimensional elasticity
==========================================================================

MATLAB code for high-order unsymmetric (Petrov-Galerkin) spectral elements
for linear plane elasticity: static, transient, modal and frequency-domain
analysis.

The element combines parametric test functions (Lagrange polynomials of
degree p on Gauss-Lobatto-Legendre nodes, conforming) with metric trial
functions (Lagrange polynomials in corotational skew coordinates, complete
in Cartesian coordinates and frame-invariant). It reproduces every
displacement field of total degree <= p exactly on arbitrarily distorted
meshes (angular and curved-edge distortion) and generalizes the unsymmetric
8-node element of Rajendran & Liew (2003) and Rajendran (2010) to arbitrary
polynomial degree.


DOCUMENTATION
-------------

The documentation is written in LaTeX (figures in TikZ):

    docs/usem-documentation.tex      main document
    docs/chapters/                   theory, getting started, ABAQUS input
                                     files, code reference, analyses and time
                                     integration, test suite, known issues,
                                     literature
    docs/figures/                    TikZ figures

Build the PDF (TeX Live or MiKTeX with biber):

    cd docs
    latexmk -pdf usem-documentation.tex

The bibliography is literature/references.bib. The literature PDFs are not
distributed (copyright).


QUICK START
-----------

    cd code
    Start_Sim          % static Lee & Bathe cubic patch test on a distorted
                       % mesh, p = 3

The model is defined in an ABAQUS input file (code/InputFilesAbaqus); the
parameters (degree, analysis type, mass matrix, time integration, ...) are set
at the top of Start_Sim.m. Requirements: MATLAB R2018b or newer; the Parallel
Computing Toolbox is optional (parallel element assembly).


TESTS
-----

    cd tests
    run_tests          % about 630 tests, roughly 2 minutes, base MATLAB only

GitHub Actions runs the suite on every push (.github/workflows/tests.yml).


REPOSITORY LAYOUT
-----------------

    code/Start_Sim.m             main script (settings, input, analysis)
    code/InputFilesAbaqus/       example ABAQUS input files (Lee & Bathe tests)
    code/subroutines/            element technology, assembly, boundary
                                 conditions, solvers, time integrators, plots
    docs/                        documentation (LaTeX)
    tests/                       test suite (matlab.unittest)
    literature/references.bib    bibliography


